WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.275
Retirement is the last wave, and it
happens one authority at a time.

2
00:00:04.275 --> 00:00:08.196
The gate is strict: cutover done,
thirty days with no incidents,

3
00:00:08.196 --> 00:00:11.425
and everything that stays
documented and running.

4
00:00:11.425 --> 00:00:15.138
Even then, the addresses where
certificates check their status

5
00:00:15.138 --> 00:00:18.850
keep serving until the last
certificate they cover has expired.

6
00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:23.238
Under the recommended design, the root
that signed the cloud issuer stays.

7
00:00:23.238 --> 00:00:28.090
And the authority's records carry their
own federal retention, measured in years,

8
00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:32.000
so the records officer signs off
before any archive is destroyed.

9
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.764
The decision for the sponsor and CIO:
retire each authority only after its

10
00:00:36.764 --> 00:00:41.762
gate passes, keeping one for domain
controllers until the last of them is gone.

11
00:00:41.762 --> 00:00:43.130
Now, the risks.
